    "summary": "Woven somelelu (sombrero or Padre&#039;s hat).\r\nThe hat is likely made from bulrush and sedge, materials used most commonly amongst the Obispeño Chumash/ Chumash in the San Luis Obispo region, although materials or the maker could have moved or been influenced by Obispeño techniques.\r\nSomelelu is Barbareño/Šmuwič Chumash word for sombrero.\r\nIt was likely woven to the right by a right-handed weaver, and the outside of the hat was the workside (conversations with Chumash weavers and basketry experts, 2023/2024).",
